Neon containers (M6): DevTools act on the inspected tab's storage partition.

- Network.clearBrowserCache clears the target's partition, not every
  partition (content/browser/devtools/protocol/network_handler.cc).
- Storage.getCookies, setCookies and clearCookies on a page or worker target
  use that target's partition like the other Storage methods; the browser
  target keeps the default one (storage_handler.cc).
- A frame's DevTools auto-attach only to service workers of the frame's own
  partition. The same scope can have a worker in every container, and DevTools
  on one tab attached to all of them, so "Clear browser cookies" and "Clear
  browser cache" in the Network panel reached other spaces
  (frame_auto_attacher.cc).
- "Empty cache and hard reload" (IDC_RELOAD_CLEARING_CACHE) clears the active
  tab's partition only (chrome/browser/ui/browser_commands.cc).

The three content/ hooks have no chrome/ alternative: the handlers and the
auto-attacher are content's own, and the protocol definition is untouched.
